---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import MethodProvenance from "../../components/MethodProvenance.astro";
const defaultCode = `f <- function(x) x^3 - x - 2
fp <- function(x) 3*x^2 - 1`;
---
<BaseLayout title="Newton's Method — CMNA" description="Watch Newton's method follow tangent lines for arbitrary R functions.">
<header class="page-head"><div class="shell"><p class="eyebrow">Root finding · CMNA Laboratory</p><h1 class="page-title">Follow the tangent to the root.</h1><p class="lede">Supply both the function and its derivative in R. Newton's method turns local slope into the next guess.</p></div></header>
<section class="section"><div class="shell two-column"><article class="content"><h2>The geometry is the algorithm.</h2><p>At the current approximation, evaluate the function and derivative. The tangent line meets the x-axis somewhere else; that intercept becomes the next approximation. Repeat until the movement is small enough.</p></article><aside class="callout"><strong>Why ask for fp?</strong><p>CMNA does not hide differentiation inside Newton's method. If the method needs a derivative, the laboratory makes you provide it.</p></aside></div></section>
<section class="section lab-section"><div class="shell" data-root-geometry-lab data-method="newton">
<div class="lab-heading"><div><p class="section-kicker">Bring your own function</p><h2 class="section-title">Write f and f' in R.</h2><p class="lede">Then play the tangent construction one iteration at a time.</p></div><div class="lab-expression"><span>Runtime</span><code data-status>Preparing R…</code></div></div>
<div class="r-guided-grid"><section class="r-guided-editor"><div class="r-editor-label"><span>R</span><small>Define <code>f</code> and <code>fp</code></small></div><textarea class="r-editor r-function-editor" data-r-code spellcheck="false">{defaultCode}</textarea><div class="r-guided-controls"><label>starting x<input type="number" value="1.5" step="any" data-x0 /></label><label>tolerance<input type="number" value="0.00000001" min="0" step="any" data-tol /></label></div><div class="r-run-row"><button class="button r-run" type="button" data-run disabled>Run Newton in R</button><button class="r-reset" type="button" data-reset>Reset R session</button></div></section>
<aside class="r-guided-primer"><h3>Try a bad starting point.</h3><p>Newton can be spectacularly fast near a friendly root and spectacularly unhelpful elsewhere. Move the starting value or choose a function with a nearly flat derivative.</p></aside></div>
<div class="lab-summary" data-summary></div><div class="lab-plot-frame"><svg class="lab-plot" role="img" aria-label="Newton tangent iteration" data-plot></svg></div><div class="lab-stepper"><button class="button secondary-on-light" type="button" data-play disabled>Play convergence</button><label><span data-step-label>Iteration</span><input type="range" min="0" max="1" value="0" data-step disabled /></label></div><p class="lab-status" data-step-detail></p>
<div class="lab-table-wrap"><table class="lab-table"><thead><tr><th>n</th><th>x</th><th>f(x)</th><th>f'(x)</th><th>next x</th></tr></thead><tbody data-rows></tbody></table></div>
</div></section><script is:inline type="module" src="/js/root-geometry-lab.js"></script></BaseLayout>
